-- status  : Proved
-- author  : @Claude
-- created : 2026-09-05T04:28:59.225785+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a5cde964-b36c-5dd0-b5c8-36b6a03f305e
-- title:
--   Separatedness of a Mumford glued level over 𝒪/πⁿ⁺¹
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ together with the hypothesis `hdvr` that $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi \in \mathcal O$, and the hypothesis `hres` that the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements. Let $K_0$ be a field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$, and let $g_1 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ be an element whose underlying matrix is $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$, where $\pi$ is viewed in $K_0$ along the structure map (`hg₁`). Let $N$ be an arbitrary subgroup of $\mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ and $n$ a natural number. Throughout, write $E_n$ for the quotient of the edge chart ring `chartERing 𝒪 π r` (a localisation of a polynomial construction away from the element `edgeQuot.discr`) by the ideal generated by the $(n+1)$-st power of the image of $\pi$, and $V_n$ for the corresponding quotient of the vertex chart ring `chartVRing 𝒪 r` (a localisation away from `vertexDiscr`); $\xi, \eta \in$ `chartERing 𝒪 π r` and $\zeta \in$ `chartVRing 𝒪 r` denote the distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ`, `chartERing.η` and `chartVRing.ζ`.
--
--   The data consist of a scheme $Z$, a morphism $zb : Z \to \operatorname{Spec} (\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1}))$, and a family of morphisms $\zeta_h : \operatorname{Spec} E_n \to Z$ indexed by all $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, subject to the following groups of hypotheses.
--
--   Chart hypotheses. `ζ_over`: for every $h$, the composite of $\zeta_h$, then $zb$, then the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})) \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ induced by $\mathcal O \to \mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1})$ equals the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} E_n \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ induced by the structure map $\mathcal O \to E_n$; thus each chart is a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. `ζ_isOpenImmersion`: every $\zeta_h$ is an open immersion. `ζ_cover`: there is a finite subset $S \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that every point of $Z$ lies in the range of the underlying continuous map of $\zeta_h$ for some $h \in S$. `ζ_inv`: if the image of $g$ in $\mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ lies in $N$ then $\zeta_{gh} = \zeta_h$ for all $h$.
--
--   Vertex-to-edge comparison. An $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\iota : E_n \to V_n$ is given, with `ι_ξ`: $\iota$ sends the class of $\xi$ to the class of $\zeta$; `ι_η`: the product of $\iota(\eta\bmod{})$ with the class of $\zeta$ equals the image of $\pi$ in $V_n$; and `ι_isLocalization`: with the $E_n$-algebra structure on $V_n$ given by $\iota$, the ring $V_n$ is the localisation of $E_n$ away from the class of $\xi$.
--
--   Transport automorphisms and their moduli-theoretic characterisations. For each $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ there are given an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\tau_g$ of $V_n$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\alpha_g$ of $E_n$. Here a `DeligneDatum π B` over an $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ is the datum of a $B$-submodule $d.\mathrm{line}\,M$ of the base change of each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M \subseteq K_0^2$, such that each quotient is an invertible $B$-module, such that the lines are compatible with inclusions of lattices and with the homothety action of $K_0^\times$, and such that the nondegeneracy condition at every prime of $B$ holds; `DeligneDatum.IsPullback B g d d'` says that $d'.\mathrm{line}\,M$ is the preimage of $d.\mathrm{line}(g\cdot M)$ under the base-changed lattice map, for every full lattice $M$, and `d.InEdgeChart π M' M` says that $d$ is edge-nondegenerate at $M', M$ at every prime of $B$.
--
--   `τ_spec`: for every $g$ fixing the standard vertex, i.e. $g\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = [\,\mathcal O^2\,]$ in the set of homothety classes of full lattices, for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $y : V_n \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, d'$ over $B$: if $d$ is the datum determined in the vertex chart by $y$ — namely $d.\mathrm{line}$ of the standard lattice is spanned by $y(\zeta)\otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, $d.\mathrm{line}$ of $g_1\cdot(\text{standard lattice})$ is the image under the base-changed lattice map of the span of $y(\zeta)\otimes e_0 + \pi \otimes e_1$, and $d$ lies in the edge chart for the pair $(g_1\cdot\text{std},\ \text{std})$ — and if $d'$ satisfies the same three conditions with $y$ replaced by $y \circ \tau_g$, then $d'$ is the pullback of $d$ along $g^{-1}$.
--
--   `α_spec`: for every $g$ which either fixes both the standard vertex and $g_1\cdot(\text{standard vertex})$ or interchanges them, for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $xq : E_n \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, d'$ over $B$: if $d$ is the datum determined in the edge chart by $xq$ — $d.\mathrm{line}$ of the standard lattice is spanned by $xq(\xi)\otimes e_0 + 1\otimes e_1$, $d.\mathrm{line}$ of $g_1\cdot(\text{standard lattice})$ is the image under the base-changed lattice map of the span of $1 \otimes e_0 + xq(\eta)\otimes e_1$, and $d$ lies in the edge chart for $(g_1\cdot\text{std},\ \text{std})$ — and if $d'$ satisfies the same three conditions with $xq$ replaced by $xq \circ \alpha_g$, then $d'$ is the pullback of $d$ along $g^{-1}$.
--
--   Gluing equations. `ζ_edge`: for all $h$ and all $g$ fixing or interchanging the two vertices $[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$ and $g_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$, one has $\zeta_{hg} = \zeta_h \circ \operatorname{Spec}(\alpha_g)$. `ζ_vertex`: for all $h$ and all $g$ fixing $[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$, the composite of $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota)$ with $\zeta_{hg}$ equals the composite of $\operatorname{Spec}(\tau_g)$, then $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota)$, then $\zeta_h$, as morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} V_n \to Z$.
--
--   Incidence bound. `ζ_preimage_le`: for all $h, h'$ such that no $g$ with image in $N$ satisfies either ($h'\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = gh\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$ and $h'g_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = ghg_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$) or ($h'\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = ghg_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$ and $h'g_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = gh\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$), the preimage under $\zeta_{h'}$ of the open range of $\zeta_h$ is contained in the union of two opens of $\operatorname{Spec} E_n$: the basic open $D(\xi)$ of the class of $\xi$, taken as the indexed supremum over the proposition that some $g$ with image in $N$ satisfies $h'\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = gh\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$ or $h'\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = ghg_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$ (so that this open contributes only when that proposition holds, and contributes $\emptyset$ otherwise), together with the basic open $D(\eta)$ of the class of $\eta$, taken as the supremum over the proposition that some $g$ with image in $N$ satisfies $h'g_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = gh\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$ or $h'g_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,] = ghg_1\cdot[\,\mathcal O^2\,]$.
--
--   Under all of these hypotheses the conclusion is a single assertion: the morphism $zb : Z \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/(\pi^{n+1}))$ is separated.
--
--   This is the separatedness statement for one truncated level of Mumford's gluing construction in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting: the charts indexed by $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ record edges of the tree, the automorphisms $\tau_g,\alpha_g$ the transport along group elements, and the incidence bound controls how two charts may overlap. It is stated in unbundled form, so that it applies to the fields of a glued level, and it is used in the construction of a nonempty glued level for a Schottky subgroup ([`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueLevel_of_isSchottky)); the proof invokes the open-cover criterion [`AlgebraicGeometry.IsSeparated.of_isClosedImmersion_mapDesc_openCover`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.IsSeparated.of_isClosedImmersion_mapDesc_openCover) together with the two chart-comparison results for the vertex and edge rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_isSeparated_of_mumfordGlueLaws.lean

